{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0c38f4cff229b019","name":"Sith Lord (CL 19)","source":{"id":"source:reference-0c38f4cff229b019","title":"Sith Lord (CL 19)","revision":25208,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:02:11Z","sha256":"4990675c6a60e74dc655fce64e1844886757ef5895871330b25ea277dc1b590c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25208","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sith%20Lord%20%28CL%2019%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0c38f4cff229b019","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Since the time of the first fallen Jedi, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Sith"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Sith","referenceId":"reference:32bde5e69837ac8e"}," have survived in one form or another for thousands of years. As the passage of time marched forward, the ancient teachings of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," were forgotten, twisted, and corrupted. Few Sith Lords, then, came from the formal training of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},", and new Sith Lords learned the methods of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," from other Sith Lords until they could rise up and claim the mantle for themselves.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although they lacked the formal instruction of their Jedi counterparts, these Sith Lords proved every bit their equal, making up for their lack of discipline with hatred and for their lack of combat training with savage brutality.\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Sith Lord Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Sith Lords should be the elite villains of your campaign. They are the undisputed masters of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},". Any Sith Lord encountered after the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ruusan"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ruusan","referenceId":"reference:68adb98c0737f8de"}," is a calculating plotter, a fiend of intrigue who hides their presence behind countless false identities and minions to ensure that they can keep working toward their goal, which is ultimately the utter destruction of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"},". A Sith Lord is unlikely to reveal themselves willingly, reserving their confession to a likely Apprentice at a time when they are most likely to turn the subject toward ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"},".\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Instead, a Sith Lord relies on a host of minions to further their agenda. The most important minion is their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Apprentice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Apprentice_(CL_13)","referenceId":"reference:a6661f4c82660f75"},", though a Sith Lord is careful to limit their time with this minion lest he create an opportunity for his Apprentice to betray them. Instead, the Sith Lord uses the Apprentice as a tool, overseeing vital missions and ensuring that their plans proceed as intended.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Beneath the Sith Apprentice, there can be any number of Dark Side thralls serving the Sith Lord, including ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Adepts"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Side_Adepts"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dark_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:4f6691195aab470e"},", and other corrupted servants. It's important to note that these servants are not technically Sith even though they are usually quite skilled in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," and might harbor the same hatred toward ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," that their Masters do. In some rare cases, a lesser minion might prove themselves worthy to replace the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Apprentice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Apprentice_(CL_13)","referenceId":"reference:a6661f4c82660f75"},", which, as their Master does with their greatest ally, is something for which the Apprentice always watches.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sith Lord Statistics (CL 19)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Noble"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Noble","referenceId":"reference:190d375ec3483f8f"}," 7/",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Apprentice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Apprentice","referenceId":"reference:580167d0bdd39739"}," 8/",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Lord"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Lord","referenceId":"reference:099f599e53fbfc32"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Destiny Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Destiny_Points"},":"]}," 2; ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 7, ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Dark Side Score"